// instant_vault_v2.kiss (step 2 version 2: Instant payments load and offload, docs/step2-load-offload-design.md)
// Purpose: the pooled vault, generic by token id: WITHDRAW (only beside a registration coin at input 0) and MERGE (anyone); NO retirement branch, no successor, nothing is ever swept
// Ports: 8 op (1 withdraw, 3 merge; anything else refused); 10 change or merged total; 12 currency (withdraw, pinned by the registration coin)
// Measured: measure/receipts/step2v2_covenant_branches.json (node 1.0.45.15 jar in-process, 8-decimal token scaling; parse, clean form and address on the live node 1.0.45.15).
// DEPLOY ONLY THE CLEAN FORM: register and spend the exact single-line text in the matching .clean.txt file (runscript clean form); the multi-line text below hashes to a different, phantom address (txn-building laws 2 and 3).
// Address of the clean form: 0xE23CA9F24CF5BDC49B75964DA145A0AE75F69E6DFD37BDCEAB5765AEB3A53413 (MxG08727WKV4J7YNN29MTCM9MGKB85EENR9SRFT6UUSTAQNCMNB799K2EU5DAJE). It names the registration address 0x5337459E075F10B5340ACF645B7815D016570787ACBF632CD5ADBB19C8F45449.
// Measured transactions (instructions per input, ! = that input refused; verdict = every input passes):
//   A_WITHDRAW_1_vault_coin: 88/31 -> valid=true (expected true)
//   A_WITHDRAW_whole_coin_no_change: 93/28 -> valid=true (expected true)
//   A_WITHDRAW_2_vault_coins: 88/31/31 -> valid=true (expected true)
